te his fear of failing.\n   - **Differentiated Instruction:** The teacher could consider differentiated instruction within the class to meet his needs. This might involve providing additional practice materials, using different teaching methods, or allowing him to demonstrate his understanding in various ways.\n   - **Parental Involvement:** Involving his parents to ensure he has support at home could also be beneficial. The teacher might suggest resources or strategies that the parents can use to help him with his math studies outside of school.\n\nIn both cases, the teacher should maintain open communication with the students, their parents, and possibly other educators to ensure that both students are set on a path that is both challenging and supportive, tailored to their individual needs and abilities."}
