ction to solidify their understanding.\n\n5. **Parental Involvement:**\n   - Involving parents can be beneficial. The teacher could suggest a meeting with the parents to discuss their child's needs and explore options together.\n\n6. **Ongoing Monitoring:**\n   - Regular check-ins with both students will help the teacher monitor their progress and adjust support as needed. This can be done through informal discussions or more structured progress reports.\n\nBy addressing both students' needs thoughtfully, the teacher can help ensure that each student is challenged appropriately and supported adequately, fostering a positive learning environment."}
