ay exhibit great rationality. Personal characteristics, life experiences, and context play significant roles in shaping how someone deals with adversity.\n\n4. **Gender Stereotypes**: These generalizations are rooted in traditional gender stereotypes, which can be limiting. Encouraging emotional expression and rational thinking across genders can lead to healthier emotional development and more effective problem-solving.\n\nIn summary, while societal norms can influence how men and boys are expected to react to challenges, it's essential to consider individual differences and move beyond stereotypes to understand the complexity of human behavior."}
