ir hand, which can be a powerful non-verbal way to show support.\n\n5. **Follow-up Support**: After the initial conversation, Donna can check in with the friend to show continued support. This could be through a text message, a phone call, or inviting them out for coffee.\n\nUltimately, the most important thing is for Donna to be genuine in her support, even if she feels uncomfortable. Her presence and willingness to stand by her friend during a difficult time can be very meaningful."}
