lving and Critical Thinking:**\n   - Present real-world problems the team has faced and ask how the candidate would approach solving them. This assesses their critical thinking and practical application of skills.\n\n6. **Soft Skills:**\n   - Evaluate communication skills, both in writing and verbally, as well as teamwork capabilities.\n   - Discuss how they handle stress and conflict, which are important for maintaining a productive work environment.\n\n7. **Questions for the Candidate:**\n   - Allow the candidate to ask questions about the role, team, and company. This provides insight into their level of interest and what they value in a workplace.\n\n8. **Closing the Interview:**\n   - Summarize the discussion and outline the next steps in the hiring process.\n   - Thank the candidate for their time and express appreciation for their interest in the role.\n\nBy covering these areas, Maria and George can make a well-rounded assessment of the candidate's capabilities and potential fit for the software engineering role."}
