.\n   - Discuss how they handle conflicts and differing opinions.\n\n3. **Adaptability:**\n   - Ask how they handle changes in project scope or technology stack.\n   - Discuss their experience learning new technologies or methodologies.\n\n### Cultural Fit\n1. **Workplace Values:**\n   - Discuss their values and how they align with the company\u2019s culture.\n   - Ask about their ideal work environment and how it compares to your company.\n\n2. **Motivation:**\n   - Ask why they are interested in this role and your company specifically.\n   - Discuss their long-term career goals and how this position fits into them.\n\n### Behavioral Questions\n1. **Problem Resolution:**\n   - Ask about a time they faced a significant challenge at work and how they resolved it.\n   - Discuss the outcome and what they learned from the experience.\n\n2. **Feedback:**\n   - Ask how they handle feedback from peers and supervisors.\n   - Discuss an example of constructive feedback they received and how they acted on it.\n\n### Closing the Interview\n1. **Candidate\u2019s Questions:**\n   - Allow the candidate to ask questions about the role, team, and company.\n   - Use their questions to gauge their interest and understanding of the position.\n\n2. **Next Steps:**\n   - Clearly outline the next steps in the hiring process.\n   - Provide a timeline for when they can expect to hear back.\n\nBy covering these areas, Maria and David can gain a comprehensive understanding of the candidate's technical abilities, experience, soft skills, and cultural fit with the company."}
