ir educational goals for their child.\n   - **Daniel**: They should explore what types of activities and lessons Daniel incorporates and how he integrates learning with play.\n\n5. **Parental Involvement**: \n   - **Dorothy**: They can ask how Dorothy encourages parental involvement and communication. Does she provide regular updates or organize parent-teacher meetings?\n   - **Daniel**: Similarly, they should inquire about Daniel's approach to involving parents in their child's education and how he communicates progress and concerns.\n\n6. **Feedback from Other Parents**: \n   - **Dorothy**: Seeking feedback from other parents whose children are currently or have been in Dorothy's class can provide valuable insights into her effectiveness and interaction with students.\n   - **Daniel**: They might want to talk to other parents about their experiences with Daniel to understand his strengths and any areas for improvement.\n\n7. **Observation and Interaction**: \n   - **Dorothy**: Arranging a visit to observe Dorothy in action and interacting with her can help the couple assess her rapport with children and her ability to manage a classroom.\n   - **Daniel**: Similarly, observing Daniel and having a conversation with him can provide firsthand experience of his teaching style and personality.\n\nBy considering these factors, the couple can make a well-rounded decision that best suits their son's needs and their family's expectations."}
