ce. Both styles have their strengths and can complement each other in a team setting, where Dorothy's analytical skills can balance Joseph's emotional insights, leading to well-rounded decision-making. Understanding and appreciating these differences can enhance collaboration, as each individual can learn from the other's strengths while working to mitigate their respective weaknesses."}
