d in extracurricular activities, volunteering, or work experience to build a well-rounded college application and develop skills that are valuable in college and beyond.\n\n7. **Personal Development**: Advice on developing time management, communication, and leadership skills might have been offered to prepare them for the independence and responsibilities that come with college life.\n\n8. **Stress Management**: The counselor could have provided tips on managing stress and maintaining a healthy balance between academics, social life, and personal well-being.\n\nBy addressing these areas, the college counselor would aim to equip John and Jennifer with the knowledge and resources they need to make informed decisions about their college journey and future careers."}
