ate her achievements, no matter how small, to build her confidence and encourage further initiative.\n\n### General Tips:\n- **Tailor Your Approach:** Recognize that each intern is unique and may require different management styles. Be flexible in your approach to meet their individual needs.\n  \n- **Foster a Collaborative Environment:** Encourage Edward and Mary to work together, leveraging Edward's leadership skills and Mary's developing abilities to create a balanced team dynamic.\n\n- **Feedback Loop:** Create a feedback loop where both interns can express their thoughts on the supervision process and suggest improvements.\n\nBy addressing the specific needs of each intern, you can help them both grow professionally and contribute effectively to the team."}
