ccesses, no matter how small, to boost her confidence.\n\n4. **Opportunities for Initiative:**\n   - Gradually assign tasks that require her to take initiative, starting with smaller responsibilities and building up to more complex ones.\n   - Encourage her to propose ideas or improvements, fostering a sense of ownership over her work.\n\n### General Strategies:\n- **Team Dynamics:**\n  - Foster a collaborative environment where Paul and Margaret can work together effectively, leveraging their strengths.\n  - Encourage open communication and team-building activities to enhance their working relationship.\n\n- **Regular Feedback:**\n  - Schedule regular one-on-one meetings with both interns to discuss their progress, challenges, and career aspirations.\n  - Use these meetings to provide feedback and adjust their development plans as needed.\n\nBy tailoring your supervision approach to their individual needs and strengths, you can help both Paul and Margaret succeed in their roles and develop valuable skills for their future careers."}
