bly even Margaret, if appropriate) could also be beneficial.\n\n3. **Set Clear Goals**: Help Brian set achievable short-term and long-term goals. This will give him a clear direction and help him stay motivated.\n\n4. **Encourage Participation**: Create opportunities for Brian to participate in team discussions and decision-making processes. This can help build his confidence and encourage a more proactive approach.\n\n5. **Positive Reinforcement**: Recognize and celebrate Brian\u2019s achievements, no matter how small. Positive reinforcement can boost his confidence and encourage him to take more initiative.\n\n### General Tips:\n- **Foster Teamwork**: Encourage collaboration between Margaret and Brian. Their different strengths can complement each other, leading to a more effective team dynamic.\n  \n- **Regular Check-ins**: Conduct regular check-ins with both interns to discuss their progress, challenges, and any support they might need.\n\n- **Adaptability**: Be open to adjusting your approach based on their feedback and evolving needs. Flexibility can help you better support their development.\n\nBy tailoring your supervision to their individual needs and leveraging their strengths, you can help both interns grow and succeed in their roles."}
