 and areas for improvement. Be specific about what she's doing well and where she can improve.\n\n4. **Encourage Questions and Participation:** Create an environment where Ruth feels comfortable asking questions and participating in discussions. This can help her feel more engaged and confident in her role.\n\n### General Tips:\n- **Foster Collaboration:** Encourage both interns to collaborate on projects where their skills complement each other. George can take the lead, while Ruth can contribute by learning and offering support.\n\n- **Monitor Progress:** Keep track of both interns' progress and adjust your strategies as needed. Regular one-on-one meetings can help you understand their individual experiences and address any challenges they face.\n\n- **Celebrate Achievements:** Recognize and celebrate their achievements, no matter how small. This can boost morale and motivate them to continue improving.\n\nBy tailoring your approach to each intern's strengths and needs, you can help them both develop into valuable team members."}
