*Skill Development**: Identify specific areas where Ruth needs development and provide resources or training opportunities to help her grow. This could be through workshops, online courses, or on-the-job training.\n\n### For Both:\n1. **Regular Check-Ins**: Schedule regular meetings to discuss their progress, provide feedback, and address any concerns or questions they might have.\n\n2. **Goal Setting**: Work with each intern to set clear, achievable goals for their internship. Regularly review these goals to track progress and make adjustments as needed.\n\n3. **Team Integration**: Encourage collaboration between Mark and Ruth. Assign them to work together on projects where Mark can lead and Ruth can contribute under guidance, fostering a supportive learning environment.\n\n4. **Feedback Loop**: Create an open feedback loop where interns feel comfortable sharing their thoughts and experiences. This can help you adjust your supervision approach to better meet their needs.\n\nBy recognizing and nurturing their individual strengths and areas for development, you can create a positive and productive internship experience for both Mark and Ruth."}
