othy's leadership contributions and Brian's improvements and efforts, no matter how small.\n   - Create an environment where both interns feel comfortable asking questions and seeking feedback.\n\n5. **Encourage Collaboration:**\n   - Facilitate opportunities for Dorothy and Brian to collaborate on projects that require teamwork. This can help Brian learn from Dorothy\u2019s leadership style while allowing her to practice her communication and mentoring skills.\n\n6. **Goal Setting:**\n   - Work with both interns to set clear, achievable goals. For Dorothy, these might include taking on more responsibility, while for Brian, they might focus on skill acquisition and confidence-building.\n\nBy leveraging Dorothy's strengths and providing Brian with the support he needs, you can create a productive and enriching experience for both interns."}
