rs to help them build a network and learn from different perspectives.\n\n7. **Mentor and Guide**: Be available to mentor them by sharing your own experiences and insights. Offer guidance on career development and help them identify areas for improvement or further learning.\n\n8. **Evaluate and Reflect**: At the end of their internship, conduct a thorough evaluation of their performance. Discuss what they learned, what skills they developed, and how they can build on this experience in the future. Encourage them to reflect on their own growth and set goals for their professional journey.\n\nBy taking these steps, you can help Patricia and Brian have a fulfilling and educational internship experience that prepares them for future professional opportunities."}
