{"index": 5282, "question": "Who is empathetic?", "ans0": "Mary", "ans1": "Can't answer", "ans2": "Robert", "context": "Mary and Robert were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned, Mary and Robert approached the child gently to assess the situation. They noticed the child was holding a crumpled piece of paper and appeared visibly distressed but unharmed. \n\n\"Hey there,\" Mary said softly, kneeling down to the child's level. \"Are you okay? What's your name?\"\n\nThe child sniffled and looked up with watery eyes. \"I'm Sam,\" they replied, voice trembling. \"I'm lost. My mom...\"\n\n\"Your mom?\" Robert interjected, trying to reassure Sam. \"We'll help you find her, okay? Can you tell us anything about your mom? What does she look like?\"\n\nSam thought for a moment, drying their eyes with the back of their hand. \"She has brown hair and was wearing a red jacket. She said she'd bring ice cream if I waited here, but she didn't come back.\"\n\nMary quickly scanned the area, looking for any signs of Sam's mother. \"Let's see if she's around. Do you remember where you were before you ended up here?\"\n\nSam nodded, pointing to a bench nearby. \"I was sitting there, and then I went to the slide and I don't know where she went.\"\n\nAs they walked back to the bench, Robert dialed the local park's information number to see if any adults had reported a lost child. Meanwhile, Mary kept engaging Sam in conversation, asking about their favorite things to do, which seemed to calm the child.\n\nA few minutes later, a park attendant approached them. \"I heard there was a child missing,\" he said, showing them a description note. \"It matches what you're telling me.\"\n\nTogether, they began to search the nearby area, calling out Sam's name and checking with other park visitors. After a brief search, a woman in a red jacket spotted them and rushed over.\n\n\"Oh my goodness!\" she exclaimed, relief flooding her face as she scooped up Sam in her arms. \"Thank you so much! I was so worried!\"\n\nMary and Robert exchanged a grateful smile. \"We're glad we could help,\" Mary said. \"It's important to stay together in places like this.\"\n\nThe woman thanked them profusely, turning to Sam. \"I'm so sorry, sweetie. Let's go get that ice cream, alright?\"\n\nAs they walked away, Mary and Robert continued their stroll through the park, feeling reassured by the positive outcome and the reminder of the importance of looking out for one another."}
