{"index": 5284, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Mary", "ans1": "Robert", "ans2": "Can't be determined", "context": "Robert and Mary were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned for the child's well-being, Robert and Mary approached cautiously. They noticed the child, a little girl around five years old, sitting on a swing, her tears soaking her cheeks. The playground was mostly empty, with only a few distant parents visible.\n\n\"Hey there,\" Robert said softly, kneeling down to the girl's level. \"Are you okay?\"\n\nThe little girl sniffled, clutching a stuffed animal tightly. \"I can't find my mom,\" she replied, her voice trembling.\n\nMary reached out and gently took the girl's hand. \"Don't worry, sweetie. We're here to help you.\"\n\nRobert spoke reassuringly, \"Do you remember where your mom was last? Maybe we can find her together.\"\n\nThe girl nodded slowly, wiping her eyes with the back of her hand. \"She was talking to someone near the slide before I went over to the swings.\"\n\nThankfully, other parents had started to notice the commotion and were gathering nearby, offering to assist. Robert and Mary, along with the concerned parents, decided to split up to cover more ground. They approached a few people near the slide, asking if they'd seen a little girl with her mother.\n\nAs they were searching, a woman emerged from the nearby bushes. \"Oh my goodness, is this little Emma?\" she exclaimed, her voice filled with relief. \"Thank you so much for finding her!\"\n\nThe girl's mother quickly scooped Emma into her arms, hugging her tightly. \"I'm so sorry, darling. I just stepped away for a moment.\"\n\nMary smiled as they saw the grateful expression on the mother's face. \"It's okay,\" she reassured. \"We're just glad you're both safe.\"\n\nRobert added, \"It's always important to look out for each other. I'm glad we could help.\"\n\nWith tears of relief in her eyes, the mother thanked Robert and Mary profusely, promising to be more careful in the future. As they watched the family leave the park, Robert and Mary felt a sense of warmth, knowing they had made a difference that day."}
