{"index": 5288, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Mary", "ans1": "Mark", "ans2": "Unknown", "context": "Mary and Mark were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned for the child's well-being, Mary and Mark approached cautiously. The child, a little girl no more than four years old, was sitting on a bench, her tears soaking her cheeks. Her small hands were wrapped tightly around a stuffed animal, which seemed to be her only source of comfort.\n\nMary knelt down to the girl's level and gently asked if she was okay. The little girl sniffled and nodded, but her eyes were red and swollen from crying. Mark, meanwhile, scanned the playground and surrounding area, noticing that there were no other adults in sight.\n\nThe girl, who introduced herself as Lucy, explained that she was waiting for her mom, who left her there for just a minute to buy some ice cream. However, her mom had not returned, and Lucy didn't know where to go. Mary and Mark reassured her that they would help find her mom.\n\nThey decided to check nearby shops and ask if anyone had seen Lucy's mother. As they walked towards the small ice cream shop located at the edge of the park, Mary and Mark noticed a woman inside who seemed very anxious. She matched the description Lucy had given them of her mother\u2014a middle-aged woman with short brown hair and a red jacket.\n\nMary approached the woman, introducing herself and Mark, and explained the situation. The woman's face lit up with relief as she recognized Lucy's picture from the phone in her hand. She explained that she had been distracted by a phone call and, in her worry, hadn't realized how much time had passed.\n\nWith heartfelt thanks, she took Lucy into her arms, promising never to leave her alone again. Mary and Mark watched as they walked away, relieved and happy that Lucy was safe.\n\nAs they resumed their walk, Mary and Mark reflected on the importance of being attentive a