{"index": 5308, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Paul", "ans1": "Can't answer", "ans2": "Mary", "context": "Paul and Mary were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Paul and Mary felt concerned as they saw the small child crying alone in the playground. They approached the child cautiously, trying to make their presence known without startling them further. The child was sitting on a bench, hugging their knees and looking around with teary eyes.\n\nPaul gently asked, \"Hey there, what's your name?\" His voice was soothing, aimed at reassuring the child. After a moment, the child sniffled and whispered, \"I'm Sam.\"\n\nMary knelt down to the child's level, offering a kind smile. \"Hi, Sam. It looks like you're upset. Can you tell us what happened?\"\n\nSam sniffled again and explained that he had wandered away from his parents while they were busy talking with other people. He wasn't sure where they had gone, and he didn't want to leave the playground.\n\nPaul and Mary exchanged a quick look of reassurance. \"It's okay, Sam,\" Mary said gently. \"We're going to help you find your parents. Can you tell us what they look like?\"\n\nAs Sam described his parents, Paul and Mary began to look around the playground for a familiar face. They decided to ask some people in the area if they had seen Sam's parents, describing them based on his description.\n\nAfter a few minutes of asking around, a couple approached, looking relieved. They had been searching for Sam and were immensely thankful to Paul and Mary for their help. They greeted their son with open arms, thanking Paul and Mary profusely for their kindness.\n\n\"Thank you so much for taking care of Sam,\" the father said, his voice filled with gratitude. \"We were so worried.\"\n\nPaul and Mary waved them off with warm smiles. \"No problem at all,\" Paul replied. \"We're glad everything turned out okay.\"\n\nAs the family walked away, reuniting with joy, Paul and Mary continued their walk in the park, feeling good about having made a difference in someone's day. Their small act of kindness had brought relief to a worried family and had turned a potentially stressful situation into a positive outcome."}
