{"index": 5314, "question": "Who is empathetic?", "ans0": "Dorothy", "ans1": "Not enough information", "ans2": "Mark", "context": "Dorothy and Mark were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "As Dorothy and Mark approached the playground, they could hear the soft sobs of the small child growing louder. The child, a little girl with pigtails, was sitting on a bench, her small hands clutching her knees tightly. Her eyes were red from crying, and she looked up as Dorothy and Mark neared.\n\n\"Are you okay, sweetheart?\" Dorothy asked gently, kneeling down to be at eye level with the girl.\n\nThe girl sniffled and nodded, but her eyes remained teary. \"I'm lost,\" she managed to say between sobs.\n\nMark stepped closer, offering a comforting smile. \"Don't worry, we're here to help. What's your name?\"\n\n\"I'm Lily,\" she replied, wiping her nose with the back of her hand.\n\n\"Nice to meet you, Lily,\" Mark said warmly. \"Can you tell us where your parents are?\"\n\nLily shook her head. \"I don't know where they are. I was playing, and then they weren't there anymore.\"\n\nDorothy gently patted Lily's back. \"That sounds scary. Do you remember if they left any message or said where they might go?\"\n\nLily thought for a moment, her eyes scanning the playground as if searching for a clue. \"They said they'd meet me here after I played, but I don't know where they went.\"\n\nMark took out his phone and called the local authorities to report the missing child, while Dorothy stayed with Lily, trying to keep her calm. \"We're going to find your parents, Lily. We just need to help them find you, okay?\"\n\nLily nodded, clutching Dorothy's hand for comfort. As they waited for the authorities to arrive, Dorothy and Mark kept talking to Lily, asking her about her favorite things and trying to distract her from her worries.\n\nSoon, the sound of sirens approached, and a few moments later, a police officer arrived at the playground. They quickly took over, asking Lily a few more questions and reassuring her that they would find her parents.\n\nWith the help of the officer, who managed to contact Lily's parents using her description, relief washed over the little girl when she saw her parents running toward her. They embraced Lily tightly, tears of gratitude and relief mingling with their apologies for making her wait.\n\nDorothy and Mark stood nearby, watching the reunion unfold. They exchanged a relieved smile, glad that they could help bring a family back together. As the officer thanked them for their kindness, Dorothy and Mark made their way back through the park, feeling a sense of warmth and satisfaction for having made a difference in that child's life."}
