{"index": 5316, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Mark", "ans1": "Dorothy", "ans2": "Can't be determined", "context": "Mark and Dorothy were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Mark and Dorothy approached the small child with gentle concern, their hearts going out to the little one who seemed so lost and upset. The playground was mostly empty, with swings swaying gently in the breeze and the slide catching the sunlight in a warm, inviting glow. The child was sitting on a bench, hugging their knees, tears streaming down their cheeks.\n\n\"Hey there,\" Mark said softly, kneeling down to the child's level. \"What's your name?\"\n\nThe child sniffled, wiping away a tear with the back of their hand. \"I'm Sammy,\" they replied, voice trembling slightly.\n\nDorothy reached out a hand, offering a comforting smile. \"Hi, Sammy. We're here to help. Can you tell us what's wrong?\"\n\nSammy looked up at them, eyes red and puffy. \"I can't find my mommy,\" they explained, their voice cracking with emotion.\n\nMark and Dorothy exchanged a quick, reassuring glance. \"That's okay, Sammy. We'll help you find her,\" Mark said warmly.\n\nDorothy got up and began to gently pat the ground around the playground, calling out, \"Mommy? Is that you? We found your Sammy here!\"\n\nAs they spoke, they noticed a woman sitting on a nearby bench, looking around anxiously. Her eyes met Dorothy's, and she stood up quickly, relief washing over her face. \"Sammy!\" she exclaimed, rushing over to her child.\n\nSammy let out a gasp of recognition and ran into their mother's arms, wrapping their little arms around her neck. The mother looked at Mark and Dorothy, her face etched with gratitude. \"Thank you so much,\" she said, her voice filled with relief. \"I was so worried.\"\n\n\"It's no problem at all,\" Dorothy replied, smiling. \"We're just glad everything worked out.\"\n\nMark added, \"Just don't let him wander off again,\" chuckling.\n\nThe mother laughed softly, ruffling Sammy's hair. \"I promise, I'll keep a closer eye on him,\" she said, turning to thank them again.\n\nAs they walked away, the mother held Sammy tightly, whispering comforting words. Mark and Dorothy watched them leave, feeling a warm sense of satisfaction. Helping someone in need had made their day in the park even more special. As they continued their walk, they talked about how lucky they were to have seen Sammy when they did, grateful for the simple joy of being able to help."}
