{"index": 5332, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Can't be determined", "ans1": "Kenneth", "ans2": "Dorothy", "context": "Kenneth and Dorothy were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned for the child's well-being, Kenneth and Dorothy approached cautiously. The child, about four years old, was clutching a teddy bear and appeared frightened. Dorothy knelt down to the child's level and gently asked, \"Hi there, are you okay? What's your name?\"\n\nThe child sniffled and looked up with big, teary eyes. \"I'm Lucy,\" she said softly. \"I can't find my mom.\"\n\nKenneth patted his leg, signaling that they were there to help. \"That's okay, Lucy. We're here to help you find your mom. Can you tell us where you saw her last?\"\n\nLucy nodded and pointed towards a nearby picnic area. \"She was eating an ice cream and talking to a man.\"\n\nDorothy and Kenneth thanked Lucy for the information and promised to find her mom as quickly as possible. They walked together to the picnic area, keeping an eye on Lucy to make sure she felt safe.\n\nAs they approached, they spotted a woman sitting at a table with a man, both engrossed in conversation. The woman looked up and gasped upon seeing Lucy. \"Lucy!\" she exclaimed, rushing over and enveloping her in a warm hug.\n\nTears of relief streamed down Lucy's face as she clung to her mom. \"Mommy, I was scared!\" she sobbed.\n\nThe woman, clearly relieved, thanked Kenneth and Dorothy profusely. \"Thank you so much for bringing her back to me. I was so worried!\"\n\nDorothy smiled, feeling glad they could help. \"I'm just glad everything turned out okay. Is there anything else we can do?\"\n\n\"No, you've done more than enough,\" the woman replied, giving their hands a heartfelt squeeze. \"Thank you again.\"\n\nWith the family reunited and Lucy safe, Kenneth and Dorothy continued their walk in the park, feeling a sense of satisfaction from helping a stranger in need."}
