{"index": 5336, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Can't be determined", "ans1": "Dorothy", "ans2": "Robert", "context": "Dorothy and Robert were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Dorothy and Robert approached the small child cautiously, wanting to ensure the child felt safe and comforted. The playground was quiet, with only their footsteps breaking the silence. As they neared, they could see the child huddled on a bench, tears streaming down their cheeks.\n\n\"Hey there,\" Dorothy said softly, kneeling down to the child's level. \"Are you okay?\" She tried to sound gentle and reassuring.\n\nThe child sniffled and nodded, wiping at their eyes with the back of one hand. \"I-I can't find my mommy.\"\n\nRobert chimed in with a warm smile, trying to ease the child's distress. \"That sounds really scary. Do you remember where you were playing before you couldn't find her?\"\n\nThe child thought for a moment, still sniffling. \"I was on the swing, and then I just couldn't see her anymore.\"\n\nDorothy suggested they try to look for the child's mother together. \"Would you like to help us look? We'll find your mommy.\"\n\nThe child nodded eagerly. \"Okay.\"\n\nDorothy and Robert stood up, holding out their hands to the child. \"Let's go look together,\" Dorothy said, extending a hand to help the child up.\n\nThe three of them began to walk slowly around the playground, checking under the slides, around the play structures, and near the benches. Dorothy and Robert encouraged the child to point out where they had last seen their mother, keeping their tone calm and supportive.\n\nAs they walked, Robert noticed a familiar woman on the other side of the playground, looking around with concern. He caught her eye and gave a quick thumbs-up. She seemed to relax a bit, and then she started walking toward them, waving.\n\n\"Mommy!\" the child shouted, breaking into a run.\n\nThe mother quickly scooped up her child, hugging them tightly. \"Oh, thank you so much!\" she said to Dorothy and Robert, her voice filled with relief.\n\n\"You're welcome,\" Dorothy replied, smiling. \"We're just glad everything turned out okay.\"\n\nRobert added, \"It's always good to help out where we can.\"\n\nThe mother thanked them again, and the three of them exchanged goodbyes. As Dorothy and Robert walked away, they felt a warm sense of satisfaction, knowing they had made a difference in someone's day."}
