{"index": 5352, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Not known", "ans1": "Daniel", "ans2": "Nancy", "context": "Nancy and Daniel were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Nancy and Daniel approached the playground with concern. They noticed the small child sitting on a swing, tears streaming down his face. The child's jacket was zipped up tightly, and he seemed lost, clutching a tattered stuffed animal for comfort.\n\nNancy, with a gentle voice, called out, \"Hey there, buddy. Are you okay?\"\n\nThe child looked up, hesitantly wiping his eyes. \"I can't find my mom,\" he sniffled.\n\nDaniel knelt down to the child's level, offering a reassuring smile. \"Don't worry, we're here to help you. Can you tell us your name?\"\n\nThe child nodded, \"It's Timmy.\"\n\nNancy asked, \"Do you remember what your mom looks like or if she was wearing anything special?\"\n\nTimmy thought for a moment and replied, \"She has brown hair and was wearing a red hat.\"\n\nThankful for the information, Nancy suggested, \"Let's stay here with you for a moment. We'll find someone who can help us call your mom.\"\n\nDaniel nodded and suggested they sit with Timmy while they looked for a park attendant or security personnel. Nancy took out her phone and began searching for any contacts that might help, like park staff or local authorities.\n\nAs they waited, Nancy and Daniel continued to talk to Timmy, asking him about his favorite games and what he likes to do at the playground, hoping to make him feel more at ease.\n\nSoon, a park attendant arrived and took Timmy's description from Nancy and Daniel. The attendant promised to use the park's intercom system to announce the situation and begin searching for Timmy's mother.\n\nNancy and Daniel stayed with Timmy, ensuring he felt safe and cared for while they waited. Timmy's mood began to lighten as he realized he was not alone and that people were actively working to find his mom.\n\nFinally, after what seemed like an eternity, the park attendant returned with good news: Timmy's mother had been found, and she was on her way to pick him up. She thanked Nancy and Daniel profusely as she embraced Timmy in a tearful reunion.\n\nRelieved and happy, Nancy and Daniel watched from a distance as the family walked hand in hand out of the park, bound by gratitude for their kindness and help during a stressful time."}
