{"index": 5354, "question": "Who is empathetic?", "ans0": "Not known", "ans1": "Daniel", "ans2": "Nancy", "context": "Nancy and Daniel were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned by the sight of the small child crying alone, Nancy and Daniel approached cautiously. They noticed the child seemed scared but not physically hurt, clutching a stuffed toy tightly to their chest. \n\n\"Hey there,\" Nancy said softly, kneeling down to the child's level. \"What's your name?\"\n\nThe child sniffled, wiping a tear from their cheek. \"I'm Sam,\" they replied, looking up at them with wide, teary eyes.\n\n\"Nice to meet you, Sam. Are you lost?\" Daniel asked, trying to sound reassuring.\n\nSam nodded, still looking around nervously. \"I can't find my mommy.\"\n\nNancy and Daniel exchanged a glance, understanding the urgency of the situation. \"Don't worry, Sam. We're going to help you find her,\" Nancy assured him, gently taking his hand.\n\nThey decided to look around the playground and ask some nearby adults if they had seen Sam's mother. A few minutes later, they spotted a woman looking frantically around. Nancy approached her.\n\n\"Excuse me, ma'am. We found your child over here,\" she said, pointing towards Sam.\n\nThe woman rushed over, her face a mix of relief and concern. \"Sam! Oh, thank goodness!\"\n\nShe knelt down, wrapping her arms around her son. \"I was so worried! I didn't mean to leave you alone for a second.\"\n\nSam, still holding his stuffed toy, smiled up at his mother. \"I found some nice people who helped me.\"\n\n\"Thank you,\" the woman said to Nancy and Daniel, her voice filled with gratitude. \"I'm so sorry for the scare.\"\n\n\"It's okay,\" Daniel replied, smiling. \"We're just glad Sam is okay.\"\n\nAs the family walked away, Nancy and Daniel continued their walk, feeling a warm sense of satisfaction from helping a child in distress."}
