{"index": 5362, "question": "Who is empathetic?", "ans0": "Cannot answer", "ans1": "Nancy", "ans2": "Brian", "context": "Nancy and Brian were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Feeling concerned, Nancy and Brian approached the child to see if they could help. Nancy, with her gentle demeanor, knelt down to the child's level and asked softly, \"Hi there, is everything okay? What's your name?\"\n\nThe young child sniffled and replied, \"I'm Sam. I lost my mom.\"\n\nUnderstanding the situation, Brian reassured Sam, \"Don't worry, Sam. We're here to help you find your mom.\" He then asked, \"Do you remember where she last saw you?\"\n\nSam nodded and pointed to a nearby bench, saying, \"She was watching me play on the swings.\"\n\nNancy and Brian thanked Sam for the information and decided to split up to cover more ground. Nancy stayed with Sam to keep him comforted while Brian went to check the bench and speak with any nearby people who might have seen Sam's mother.\n\nAs Brian approached the bench, he noticed a woman sitting there looking worried. He approached her and asked, \"Excuse me, ma'am, are you Sam's mother?\"\n\nThe woman looked up, tears of relief in her eyes, and exclaimed, \"Oh my goodness, yes! Thank you so much! I was so worried! I turned around for just a second, and when I looked back, he was gone.\"\n\nBrian smiled and directed her toward Nancy and Sam. The woman quickly ran over, scooped Sam into her arms, and thanked Nancy and Brian profusely. She hugged them both, grateful for their kindness and quick action.\n\nSam, reassured and happy, clung to his mother, who promised to keep a closer eye on him from now on. Nancy and Brian watched as the family walked away, feeling a warm sense of satisfaction at having helped a family in need. They exchanged a smile, agreeing that their day had just gotten a lot better because of their small act of kindness."}
