{"index": 5376, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Nancy", "ans1": "Christopher", "ans2": "Can't be determined", "context": "Nancy and Christopher were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned, Nancy and Christopher approached the child to see if they could help. The child, a little girl with tear-stained cheeks, was huddled on a swing, clutching a worn-out teddy bear. Nancy asked gently, \"Hey there, sweetie. What's your name, and what's making you upset?\"\n\nThe girl sniffled, responding with a small voice, \"I'm Emma. I-I can't find my mommy.\"\n\nChristopher knelt down to be at eye level with Emma and spoke softly, \"That must be really scary, Emma. Do you remember what your mom looks like, or where you last saw her?\"\n\nEmma nodded, wiping her tears, and pointed to a nearby bench where her mom might be sitting. Nancy and Christopher followed the direction she indicated, looking around the playground for any sign of Emma's mother.\n\nAfter a few moments, they spotted a woman sitting on the bench, engrossed in a book and seemingly unaware of her daughter's distress. Nancy signaled to Christopher and then approached the woman, tapping her on the shoulder.\n\n\"Excuse me, ma'am,\" Nancy said, \"we think your daughter might be over by the swings looking for you.\"\n\nThe woman looked up, her eyes widening with surprise and relief, \"Oh, thank goodness! Emma, where are you? I've been looking everywhere for you!\"\n\nEmma, hearing her mother's voice, ran over to the bench, throwing her arms around her mom's legs. The woman scooped her up into a tight hug, murmuring soothing words as Emma buried her face in her mother's neck.\n\nNancy and Christopher exchanged a relieved smile. \"Glad we could help,\" Christopher said. \"Do you need any assistance?\"\n\nThe woman nodded, still trying to catch her breath, \"Thank you so much. I had no idea how long she'd been gone. Do you mind if we keep an eye on her for a little while longer?\"\n\n\"Of course not,\" Nancy replied warmly. \"We're happy to help ensure she stays safe.\"\n\nAs Emma's mother expressed her gratitude, they all felt a sense of relief knowing the little girl was safe and reunited with her family. Nancy and Christopher watched as the family began chatting and laughing, glad they could bring some peace to a potentially distressing situation."}
