{"index": 5392, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Elizabeth", "ans1": "Can't be determined", "ans2": "George", "context": "Elizabeth and George were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Elizabeth and George approached the small child cautiously, trying to gauge the situation without alarming the child further. The playground was quiet, with only the sound of the child's soft sobs echoing slightly in the empty space. Elizabeth knelt down to the child's eye level and spoke softly, \"Hi there, sweetie. What's going on? Are you lost or hurt?\"\n\nThe child sniffled, wiping away tears with the back of a tiny hand, and replied in a quivering voice, \"I... I can't find my mommy.\"\n\nConcerned, George reached out gently and touched the child's shoulder, offering a reassuring smile. \"Don't worry, we're here to help you. Do you remember where you last saw your mom?\"\n\nThe child thought for a moment, then pointed towards the entrance of the playground. \"Over there... I was swinging, and then she went to get ice cream.\"\n\nElizabeth nodded, understanding the situation. \"Okay, we'll go and check there for her. Can you hold my hand while we look for her?\"\n\nThe child nodded eagerly, grasping Elizabeth's hand tightly, finding some comfort in the gesture. As they walked, the child began to calm down slightly, comforted by the presence of these kind strangers.\n\nThey headed towards the entrance, keeping an eye out for the child's mother. Upon reaching the area, they spotted a woman looking around anxiously. \"Is this your mom?\" Elizabeth asked, pointing towards the woman.\n\nThe child nodded, beaming as the woman's face lit up with relief upon seeing her child. \"Oh, thank goodness! I was so worried!\"\n\nThe woman approached, hugging her child tightly. \"I'm so sorry, I just went to get some ice cream, and when I came back, I couldn't find you anywhere.\"\n\nGeorge smiled, glad that they could help. \"No worries at all. Happens to the best of us. Just glad you're safe.\"\n\nThe woman thanked them profusely, and Elizabeth suggested, \"Maybe we should stick around until she's sure her little one is okay. Then you can enjoy your ice cream together.\"\n\nThe woman agreed, grateful for their vigilance. As they sat on a nearby bench, watching the child and mother enjoy a moment together, George and Elizabeth felt a warm sense of fulfillment, knowing they had helped reunite a family."}
