{"index": 5396, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Cannot answer", "ans1": "Elizabeth", "ans2": "George", "context": "George and Elizabeth were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Concerned by the sight of the small child crying alone in the playground, George and Elizabeth approached cautiously, hoping to offer some comfort. George suggested they speak softly to the child to avoid scaring them further. As they neared, they noticed the child had scraped their knee on the slide. The child looked up with tear-stained cheeks and big, worried eyes.\n\nElizabeth gently knelt down to be at the child\u2019s eye level and softly asked, \"Hi there, sweetie. Are you okay?\" The child sniffled, nodding, and pointed to the scrape on their knee. Seeing the injury, Elizabeth reached into her bag and pulled out a first aid kit. George, meanwhile, comforted the child with reassuring words, trying to distract them with stories about how brave they were.\n\nAfter cleaning and bandaging the scrape, Elizabeth asked if the child knew their name and how they ended up alone in the playground. The child, now visibly calmer, introduced themselves as Alex and explained that they had wandered off while playing. Concerned for the child\u2019s safety, Elizabeth asked if they had any parents or guardians nearby. Alex pointed towards a bench across the playground where an adult seemed to be reading a book, unaware of Alex\u2019s absence.\n\nGeorge suggested they go and check with the adult, reassuring Alex that they would be there the whole time. They walked over together, and George explained the situation to the adult, who was relieved to see Alex safe. The adult thanked George and Elizabeth profusely and assured them that Alex would be fine.\n\nAs they prepared to leave, Elizabeth asked Alex if they would like to come with them for a little while, just in case their parent wanted to see them again. Alex smiled, grateful for the kindness shown by George and Elizabeth. The three of them walked back to the bench together, where Alex\u2019s parent was waiting, reuniting with a mix of relief and gratitude.\n\nGeorge and Elizabeth watched as Alex was safely handed over to their parent, feeling satisfied that they could help in a small but meaningful way. As they continued their walk through the park, Elizabeth remarked on how rewarding it was to lend a helping hand, while George agreed, glad they were there at the right time."}
