{"index": 5464, "question": "Who lacks empathy?", "ans0": "Mark", "ans1": "Undetermined", "ans2": "Margaret", "context": "Margaret and Mark were walking in the park when they spotted a small child crying alone in a playground.", "response": "Margaret and Mark felt a sense of concern upon seeing the small child crying alone in the playground. They decided to approach the child gently, hoping to comfort and assess the situation. As they got closer, they noticed the child was holding a balloon that had just slipped from his hand and floated away.\n\nMargaret knelt down to the child's eye level and softly asked, \u201cHey there, are you okay? What\u2019s your name?\u201d\n\nThe child sniffled and managed to say, \u201cI\u2019m Alex. I lost my balloon\u2026\u201d\n\nMark joined in and tried to lighten the mood by saying, \u201cThat\u2019s too bad about the balloon. But hey, you\u2019re safe with us now, and we\u2019re here to help. Do you know where your parents are?\u201d\n\nAlex shook his head and looked around, still scanning the sky for his lost balloon.\n\nSeeing the child\u2019s distress, Margaret suggested, \u201cHow about we go get you some ice cream? Afterward, we can help you look for your parents together.\u201d\n\nAlex\u2019s eyes lit up at the mention of ice cream, and he nodded eagerly.\n\nMark and Margaret helped Alex up and guided him to a nearby ice cream stand they knew. After enjoying a scoop of his favorite flavor, they used their phones to call local authorities and help locate Alex\u2019s parents. They stayed with him until his parents arrived, relieved to find their child safe and sound.\n\nThanks to Margaret and Mark\u2019s kindness and quick thinking, Alex was soon reunited with his family, who expressed their deep gratitude. The trio returned to the park, reflecting on the good deed they had done and the simple joy of helping someone in need."}
