pings.\n\n8. **Applied Mathematics**: Real-world scenarios requiring mathematical modeling, such as designing a structure, optimizing a process, or simulating a physical system.\n\n9. **Geometry and Trigonometry**: Problems could involve spatial reasoning, geometric proofs, or trigonometric identities.\n\n10. **Logic and Reasoning**: These questions test the ability to think logically and reason through complex problems, often involving word problems or puzzles.\n\nDuring the interview, Dorothy and Williams would need to demonstrate not only their technical skills but also their ability to communicate their thought process clearly and effectively. They might be given time to write out their solutions and explain their reasoning to the interviewers."}
