romagnetism, to solve engineering problems.\n\nThese questions not only assess technical knowledge but also the ability to think critically and work under pressure. Candidates are often evaluated on their approach to solving problems, including how they break down complex issues, the clarity of their explanations, and their ability to justify their solutions."}
